1. Purpose

This software, documentation, configurations, trained-model interfaces,
evaluation code, and associated project materials (collectively, the
"Software") are provided solely for academic research, education,
reproducibility, and non-commercial scientific evaluation involving public,
properly licensed, or synthetic datasets.

The Software is a research prototype. It is not an operational biometric
identification, authentication, forensic decision-making, or security product.

2. Permission Grant

Subject to the conditions and restrictions in this License, you may:

  a. use, reproduce, study, and evaluate the Software for non-commercial
     academic research or education;
  b. modify the Software and create derivative research implementations;
  c. publish scientific results obtained with the Software; and
  d. redistribute the Software, or modified versions of it, for the same
     permitted purposes.

3. Conditions

Any use or redistribution must:

  a. retain this License and the above copyright notice;
  b. clearly identify material modifications;
  c. acknowledge this project in resulting publications, reports, posters,
     presentations, or derivative repositories, and cite the associated paper
     if and when a formal citation is provided;
  d. comply with applicable law, research-ethics requirements, dataset terms,
     privacy obligations, and institutional review requirements; and
  e. preserve the distinction between ground-truth recovery, structural
     plausibility, and predictive uncertainty. Generated content must not be
     represented as a person's true missing biometric information without
     valid supporting evidence.

4. Prohibited Uses

You may not use the Software, directly or indirectly, to:

  a. bypass, weaken, test without authorization, or defeat a biometric
     authentication or access-control system;
  b. impersonate a person, facilitate identity fraud, or generate biometric
     material intended to be accepted as belonging to a real individual;
  c. fabricate physical or digital fingerprint artefacts for presentation as
     genuine evidence or for use against a biometric sensor;
  d. identify, re-identify, surveil, track, profile, or make consequential
     decisions about individuals;
  e. deploy an operational law-enforcement, border-control, employment,
     insurance, credit, housing, educational-admission, or other high-impact
     biometric system;
  f. process biometric data without the lawful authority, permission, or
     dataset rights required for that processing;
  g. redistribute any third-party dataset obtained separately from this
     repository, except where its own license expressly permits redistribution;
     or
  h. use the Software for commercial purposes or offer it as a paid product or
     service without separate written permission from the copyright holder.

5. Dataset and Model-Weight Exclusion

This License applies only to the Software contained in this repository. It does
not grant rights to SOCOFing, NIST SD302, NIST SD303, any other third-party
dataset, or any separately distributed model weights. Each dataset and external
artefact remains governed by its own terms. No biometric dataset is included
or relicensed by this repository.

6. Research Outputs and Responsibility

Reconstructions produced by generative models may be plausible but incorrect.
Users are responsible for validating results, reporting uncertainty and failure
modes, preventing data leakage, and avoiding claims unsupported by the stated
experimental protocol. Outputs must not be treated as forensic conclusions or
evidence of identity.

